{{also|häufen}}
==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|de|Haufe}} {{i|archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|hūfe}}, from {{inh|de|goh|hūfo}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*hūpô}}, whence also {{cog|gml|hūpe}}. A related form was Middle and Old High German {{m|goh|houf}}, from
Proto-Germanic {{m|gem-pro|*haupaz}}, whence {{cog|odt|houph}} (modern {{cog|nl|hoop}}), {{cog|osx|hōp}}, {{cog|ang|hēap}} (modern {{cog|en|heap}}). The vowels of both forms merged regularly in Modern Standard German ''-au-'', but the ending ''-en'' in the modern word shows that it continues the weak {{cog|goh|hūfo}}, which was predominant in most of [[High German]].

